@LopezCastroRoberto 

Thanks for your review. I have finished the test. The MRCR on GLM-5.3 (8 needles, 4K-256K) shows no difference: 0.903 on main vs 0.890 with these PRs, paired difference -0.013 [-0.038, +0.012]; details are in the description. 

And this PR doesn't change the precision of the index scores: on SM100, DeepGEMM's MQA logits kernels already return BF16 (see [`mqa_logits_use_mx_scales()`](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/c50aca14416ef29f6ed0ed256302f30646726dcd/vllm/utils/deep_gemm.py#L597-L606)), and main only widens them to FP32 before the top-k ([`as_fp32_logits`](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/c50aca14416ef29f6ed0ed256302f30646726dcd/vllm/model_executor/layers/sparse_attn_indexer.py#L304-L305)). #40811 and #52696 rounded FP32 scores to BF16, which is a different change.

reviews.body:
We need to keep both FP32 and BF16 paths. See https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64580.

Please rebase+fix conflicts.

Can you also share more details about the kernel-wise benchmark results and the benchmarking script? Are you using `do_bench_cudagraph`? We need to make sure that there are no perf regressions. Please sweep rows {1, 4, 8, 16, 33, 64} × lengths {16K, 64K, 128K, 256K, 1M}
